     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms,sans-serif;color:#0b5394\">Hi Viviana,</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms,sans-serif;color:#0b5394\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms,sans-serif;color:#0b5394\">if you use rgl.open() before running plotRefToTarget you should get a new rgl device and the grid will then be plotted in that new device. Make sure to adjust the device settings according to your preference through the rgl.open arguments.</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms,sans-serif;color:#0b5394\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms,sans-serif;color:#0b5394\">Hope this helps,</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms,sans-serif;color:#0b5394\">All the best,</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms,sans-serif;color:#0b5394\">Antigoni</div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
